  haskoki-demo [--output json|text] compare
  haskoki-demo --help | demo --help | check --help | compare --help

Commands:
  demo      (default) keygen, then sign/verify (ECDSA P-256) and
            encrypt/decrypt (RSA-OAEP SHA256) of fixed PUBLIC fixtures,
            plus a pinned SHA-256 digest anchor. Human summary plus a
            JSON report under /out.
  check     run pkcs11-check v0.2.2 (doctor gate, then the test lane)
            against the bundle directly or via the loopback proxy shim.
            Exit 0 only on runs with zero findings; any finding lists
            separately and exits 1. Smoke/full profiles are PROVISIONAL.
  compare   run the full checker profile direct vs proxied (subset = all,
            PROVISIONAL) and diff per-test verdict transcripts. Exit 0
            only on completed runs with zero findings and zero
            unexpected diffs; findings shared by both modes are shown
            (and exit 1) but are not diffs.

Global:
  --output json|text   stdout rendering (default text). Report files are
            always machine-readable under a unique run dir in /out.
  Exit codes (exact): 0 healthy / 1 findings or unexpected diffs /
            2 usage-or-infrastructure failure.
  Demo PINs, seeds and labels are PUBLIC fixtures; values are never
  logged (command echoes redact --pin arguments).
EOF
}

demo_help() {
  cat <<'EOF'
haskoki-demo demo — fixed-fixture crypto round-trips (default command)

Usage:
  haskoki-demo [--output json|text] demo

Runs, against fresh per-run SQLite stores under a unique /out run dir:
  1. slot listing (token haskoki-demo present)
  2. EC P-256 keypairgen, ECDSA-SHA256 sign, then verify ("Signature
     is valid"); raw signature must be exactly 64 bytes
  3. SHA-256 digest of the fixed 3-byte message, byte-compared to the
     pinned FIPS constant (deterministic anchor)
  4. RSA-2048 keypairgen, RSA-OAEP-SHA256 encrypt (256-byte output),
     then decrypt; plaintext must round-trip byte-identically

Fixtures (all PUBLIC, pinned): messages `abc` and `hello-rsa`, user
and SO PINs, key labels, OAEP hash/MGF. Determinism: exit codes,
output shapes, the digest bytes and round-trip equality are fixed;
fresh key bytes, signatures and ciphertexts vary per run by design
(new randomness each invocation).

Isolated single-purpose stores per phase: this pkcs11-tool release
selects the first enumerated key for some operations, so each phase
gets a store holding only its own keys (documented, deterministic).

Exit: 0 all verifications hold / 1 a verification failed / 2 usage
or environment failure (module or /out unavailable).
EOF
}

check_help() {
  cat <<'EOF'
haskoki-demo check — pkcs11-check lane, direct or proxied

Usage:
  haskoki-demo [--output json|text] check --mode direct|proxy --profile smoke|full

Flow: resolve the module (direct: bundle libhaskoki.so; proxy: start
the loopback daemon and use its shim), run `doctor` as a hard gate,
then `test` with the profile selection. Findings (failed/error/
crashed/timeout/xpass verdicts) list separately with stable per-test
ids; the native checker exit status is preserved in the report.

Profiles are PROVISIONAL (R4 freezes; values live in
examples/release/pkcs11-check/profiles.conf):
  smoke   small fast subset: offline marker plus a -k selection over
          interface/slot/digest/profiles categories
  full    everything smoke does plus the rest of the checker surface:
          the offline marker over the whole suite

Modes: direct runs the checker against the bundle module; proxy runs
it against the proxy shim with the daemon on 127.0.0.1:17512
(HASKOKI_DEMO_PROXY_PORT overrides; one run at a time — a busy port
fails loudly). Proxy mode needs no external network (loopback only).

Exit: 0 zero findings / 1 one or more findings / 2 usage or
infrastructure failure (bad flags, doctor refusal, daemon or checker
setup error, incomplete run).
EOF
}

compare_help() {
  cat <<'EOF'
haskoki-demo compare — direct-vs-proxied verdict diff (plumbing)

Usage:
  haskoki-demo [--output json|text] compare

Runs the full checker profile twice (direct, then via the loopback
proxy shim) and diffs per-test verdict transcripts after normalizing
test ids. Findings shared by both modes are shown but are not diffs;
every outcome mismatch (including present-in-one-side-only) is an
unexpected diff. Both sub-run reports are kept under the run dir.

Subset = all (PROVISIONAL, R5 freezes the parity subset definition).

Exit: 0 both runs completed with zero findings and zero unexpected
